e minister at the time you were  david cameron's  deputy chief of staff did you ever met  meet lex greensell did you raise any  concerns about the access that he was  given  well i've been racking my brains i took  to the very best of my recollection  i never met with them but i can't say  for for sure i'd have to  to check over the the records but i have  zero recollection i'm pretty sure that i  i didn't meet with them but i think you  you raised investigation i believe that  david cameron has been uh cleared uh as  as a result of that  and uh any appropriate meetings will of  course be properly  declared and i don't there was any  change in in government policy and  certainly from working with david  cameron  over a number of years i always found  him a man of the utmost integrity and  i've no doubt that would pertain in this  situation as well  quite a lot of the allegations in the  sunday times this morning  are talking about how lex grinza was  given access through  jeremy hayward of course head of the  civil service at that point is that  something that  should raise any concerns or do you  think it merits further investigation  no i think all of these things will have  been properly declared i remember when i  worked in downing street we had very  tight restrictions about the  declarations of  meetings those would be fully in the the  public domain  uh clearly and sadly jeremy hayward is  no longer  with us but again he was somebody that  always uh abided punctiliously with the  the rules uh in relation to engaging  with with third parties  okay and just finally there's been an  outpouring of allegations about  harassment  assault abuse against uh some of  britain's leading private schools um  what's happening is there an  investigation that's taking place and  how important  is it that the government prioritizes  this  these are very serious allegations and  clearly  any child at school or indeed anyone  needs to  feel safe and if there are concerns that  people have they must raise them with  responsible adults or with the police  uh in terms of the the actual steps  being taken uh the  is the independent schools uh  investigation  uh an inspection regime and the the dfe  can call  them in and we'll we'll deal with that  as appropriate so either take measures  uh to deal with those safeguarding  issues or ultimately to to close the  school so we have those in uh  independent  inspection regimes and it's important  those uh are undertaken as appropriate  okay oliver doubt and thank you very  much for being on the show this morning  oliver dowden
 

